A plain `.test {}` class in `globals.css` isn't a Tailwind utility, so variants like `md:` can't be applied to it — `md:test` does nothing. Register it as a utility with the `@utility` directive instead:

```css
@utility test {
  background: red;
}
```

Then `md:test` will work. Source: `tailwind-css/src/docs/upgrade-guide.mdx` §"Adding custom utilities" (line 648) and `tailwind-css/src/docs/adding-custom-styles.mdx` §"Adding custom utilities" (line 410).

